	"skills": [],
	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nXGAMaWv26b8IVfR9",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 10, DX 13, IQ 5, HT 11, HP 10, WILL 10, PER 12, FP 11, SPEED 6, MOVE 12, DODGE 9, DR 0. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nSYtWZKAhKiKXYOyp",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 32 (offense 29, protection 3), threat tier standard, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "ng0GOStgLsIc6e3Xs",
			"text": "Beaks and Claws: No attack roll and no active defense. Beaks and Claws: 1d-1 piercing, Reach C. No attack roll and no defence. Ravens go for the face and the eyes by preference: roll HT or fight blinded until the swarm is driven off."
		},
		{
			"id": "n0f5aNGecU8-nmlag",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/swarm-of-ravens.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nheUAJiVO7ul-h4he",
			"text": "Independent build total: 76 points of racial traits plus 0 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "nrNcf_V4GQdMQYQ52",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Swarm of Ravens (SRD 5.1). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "n8y1PNXFdYfeKXG3z",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "nOajggbxtAZXoddIu",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 50 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "n9_mCNshXVBXysEvM",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 6; air Move 12, 18 at a sprint (primary). The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "nSId3k51Pdfw6vHKy",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "nIUn8F7XharaOQLdS",
			"text": "One hex of swarm."
		},
		{
			"id": "nkQAI-N1g29qctZh2",
			"text": "IQ 5 is the highest in the batch and deliberate: corvids plan, and a GM should play this flock as though it has an opinion about who is dangerous."
